{"question_id":"pmatch-blist-ib-with-blist-iibptable-bo-jee-main-physics-7nw1m7k7fjfvga4c","qKey":"pmatch-blist-ib-with-blist-iibptable-bo-jee-main-physics-7nw1m7k7fjfvga4c","permalink":"pmatch-blist-ib-with-blist-iibptable-bo-jee-main-physics-7nw1m7k7fjfvga4c","paperTitle":"JEE Main 2025 (Online) 7th April Evening Shift","year":2025,"subject":"physics","chapter":"heat-and-thermodynamics","type":"mcq","marks":4,"negMarks":1,"content":"<p>Match <b>List - I</b> with <b>List - II</b>.</p><table border=\"1\">\n  <tr>\n    <th>List - I</th>\n    <th>List - II</th>\n  </tr>\n  <tr>\n    <td>(A) Isothermal</td>\n    <td>(I) \u0394W (work done) = 0</td>\n  </tr>\n  <tr>\n    <td>(B) Adiabatic</td>\n    <td>(II) \u0394Q (supplied heat) = 0</td>\n  </tr>\n  <tr>\n    <td>(C) Isobaric</td>\n    <td>(III) \u0394U (change in internal energy) \u2260 0</td>\n  </tr>\n  <tr>\n    <td>(D) Isochoric</td>\n    <td>(IV) \u0394U = 0</td>\n  </tr>\n</table>\n\n<p>Choose the <b>correct</b> answer from the options given below :</p>","options":[{"identifier":"A","content":"<p>(A)-(III), (B)-(II), (C)-(I), (D)-(IV)</p>"},{"identifier":"B","content":"<p>(A)-(II), (B)-(IV), (C)-(I), (D)-(III)</p>"},{"identifier":"C","content":"<p>(A)-(IV), (B)-(II), (C)-(III), (D)-(I)</p>"},{"identifier":"D","content":"<p>(A)-(IV), (B)-(I), (C)-(III), (D)-(II)</p>"}],"correct_options":["C"],"explanation":"<p>To accurately match the terms from List-I with the corresponding statements in List-II, consider the properties of each thermodynamic process:</p>\n\n<p><p><strong>Isothermal Process (A)</strong>: </p></p>\n<p><p>During an isothermal process, the temperature remains constant (<mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -0.05ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"7.655ex\" height=\"1.67ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -716 3383.6 738\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"394\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-394\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mi\" transform=\"translate(833,0)\"><use data-c=\"1D447\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D447\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mo\" transform=\"translate(1827.8,0)\"><use data-c=\"3D\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-3D\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mn\" transform=\"translate(2883.6,0)\"><use data-c=\"30\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-30\"></use></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container>), which means that the change in internal energy (<mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -0.05ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"3.62ex\" height=\"1.67ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -716 1600 738\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"394\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-394\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mi\" transform=\"translate(833,0)\"><use data-c=\"1D448\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D448\"></use></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container>) is zero. Therefore, it corresponds to (IV).</p></p>\n<p><p><strong>Adiabatic Process (B)</strong>: </p></p>\n<p><p>In an adiabatic process, no heat is exchanged with the surroundings (<mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -0.439ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"7.823ex\" height=\"2.059ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -716 3457.6 910\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"394\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-394\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mi\" transform=\"translate(833,0)\"><use data-c=\"1D444\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D444\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mo\" transform=\"translate(1901.8,0)\"><use data-c=\"3D\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-3D\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mn\" transform=\"translate(2957.6,0)\"><use data-c=\"30\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-30\"></use></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container>). This matches with (II).</p></p>\n<p><p><strong>Isobaric Process (C)</strong>: </p></p>\n<p><p>An isobaric process involves constant pressure conditions (<mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -0.05ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"7.732ex\" height=\"1.67ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -716 3417.6 738\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"394\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-394\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mi\" transform=\"translate(833,0)\"><use data-c=\"1D443\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D443\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mo\" transform=\"translate(1861.8,0)\"><use data-c=\"3D\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-3D\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mn\" transform=\"translate(2917.6,0)\"><use data-c=\"30\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-30\"></use></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container>), but internal energy (<mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -0.05ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"3.62ex\" height=\"1.67ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -716 1600 738\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"394\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-394\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mi\" transform=\"translate(833,0)\"><use data-c=\"1D448\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D448\"></use></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container>) can change. Thus, it's associated with (III).</p></p>\n<p><p><strong>Isochoric Process (D)</strong>: </p></p>\n<p><p>For an isochoric process, volume remains constant (<mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -0.05ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"7.773ex\" height=\"1.67ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -716 3435.6 738\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"394\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-394\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mi\" transform=\"translate(833,0)\"><use data-c=\"1D449\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D449\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mo\" transform=\"translate(1879.8,0)\"><use data-c=\"3D\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-3D\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mn\" transform=\"translate(2935.6,0)\"><use data-c=\"30\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-30\"></use></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container>), which means that no work is done (<mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -0.05ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"8.404ex\" height=\"1.67ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -716 3714.6 738\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"394\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-394\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mi\" transform=\"translate(833,0)\"><use data-c=\"1D44A\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D44A\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mo\" transform=\"translate(2158.8,0)\"><use data-c=\"3D\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-3D\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mn\" transform=\"translate(3214.6,0)\"><use data-c=\"30\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-30\"></use></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container>). This aligns with (I).</p></p>\n\n<p>Based on these descriptions, t